{"explanation":"Creates the dedicated Android instrumentation test requested for EncryptedKey. The test uses only the coordinated public EncryptedKey API: retained two-argument legacy encryption/decryption, current three-argument encryption, current-record inspection, and dual-key decryption. It exercises an AndroidKeyStore AES/GCM key across creation and reload, and validates legacy records encrypted with a PBKDF2-derived AES key. The supplied API surface does not expose serialized ciphertext or retained Cipher parameters, so a non-reflective test cannot directly compare the two stored GCM nonce/parameter encodings; the repeated-write test instead proves both records remain independently decryptable after reloading the same AndroidKeyStore key.","review_assumptions":["Android instrumentation devices used for this test support AndroidKeyStore AES keys with GCM block mode and 128-bit key generation, as required by the coordinated production current-key lifecycle.","EncryptedKey's provided current/legacy API surface is complete for this test. In particular, it exposes no serialized-record, ciphertext, or Cipher-parameter accessor, so direct non-reflective assertions that two retained GCM parameter encodings differ are not possible in this file.","The production Encryptor and MasterKey APIs needed to invoke their complete lifecycle are not present in sibling_files_api_surface; this dedicated test therefore verifies their coordinated EncryptedKey record contracts directly rather than inventing constructors or methods."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyTest.java","original_code":"","edit_kind":"create","corrected_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.security.keystore.KeyGenParameterSpec;
import android.security.keystore.KeyProperties;

import androidx.test.ext.junit.runners.AndroidJUnit4;

import org.junit.Test;
import org.junit.runner.RunWith;

import java.security.KeyStore;
import java.util.UUID;

import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.SecretKeyFactory;
import javax.crypto.spec.PBEKeySpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

import static org.junit.Assert.assertArrayEquals;
import static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;
import static org.junit.Assert.assertFalse;
import static org.junit.Assert.assertNotNull;
import static org.junit.Assert.assertTrue;

@RunWith(AndroidJUnit4.class)
public class EncryptedKeyTest {
    private static final String CURRENT_KEY_ID_PREFIX = "encryptedKeyTestCurrent-";

    @Test
    public void currentRecordRoundTripsAfterAndroidKeyStoreKeyReload() throws Exception {
        String keyId = CURRENT_KEY_ID_PREFIX + UUID.randomUUID();
        KeyStore keyStore = KeyStore.getInstance("AndroidKeyStore");
        keyStore.load(null);

        try {
            SecretKey currentKey = generateCurrentKey(keyId);
            SecretKey plaintext = generateSoftwareAesKey();

            EncryptedKey encrypted = EncryptedKey.encrypt(currentKey, plaintext, keyId);

            assertTrue(encrypted.isCurrentRecord());
            assertEquals(keyId, encrypted.getWrappingKeyId());

            SecretKey reloadedCurrentKey = (SecretKey) keyStore.getKey(keyId, null);
            assertNotNull(reloadedCurrentKey);

            SecretKey decrypted = encrypted.decrypt(generateSoftwareAesKey(), reloadedCurrentKey);
            assertSecretKeyEquals(plaintext, decrypted);
        } finally {
            if (keyStore.containsAlias(keyId)) {
                keyStore.deleteEntry(keyId);
            }
        }
    }

    @Test
    public void repeatedCurrentRecordsDecryptWithTheSameReloadedAndroidKeyStoreKey() throws Exception {
        String keyId = CURRENT_KEY_ID_PREFIX + UUID.randomUUID();
        KeyStore keyStore = KeyStore.getInstance("AndroidKeyStore");
        keyStore.load(null);

        try {
            SecretKey currentKey = generateCurrentKey(keyId);
            SecretKey firstPlaintext = generateSoftwareAesKey();
            SecretKey secondPlaintext = generateSoftwareAesKey();

            EncryptedKey firstRecord = EncryptedKey.encrypt(currentKey, firstPlaintext, keyId);
            EncryptedKey secondRecord = EncryptedKey.encrypt(currentKey, secondPlaintext, keyId);

            SecretKey reloadedCurrentKey = (SecretKey) keyStore.getKey(keyId, null);
            assertNotNull(reloadedCurrentKey);
            assertSecretKeyEquals(
                    firstPlaintext,
                    firstRecord.decrypt(generateSoftwareAesKey(), reloadedCurrentKey));
            assertSecretKeyEquals(
                    secondPlaintext,
                    secondRecord.decrypt(generateSoftwareAesKey(), reloadedCurrentKey));
        } finally {
            if (keyStore.containsAlias(keyId)) {
                keyStore.deleteEntry(keyId);
            }
        }
    }

    @Test
    public void legacyRecordEncryptedWithPbkdf2DerivedKeyRemainsDecryptable() throws Exception {
        SecretKey legacyKey = deriveLegacyAesKey("legacy password".toCharArray());
        SecretKey plaintext = generateSoftwareAesKey();

        EncryptedKey legacyRecord = EncryptedKey.encrypt(legacyKey, plaintext);

        assertFalse(legacyRecord.isCurrentRecord());
        assertSecretKeyEquals(plaintext, legacyRecord.decrypt(legacyKey));
    }

    private static SecretKey generateCurrentKey(String keyId) throws Exception {
        KeyGenerator generator = KeyGenerator.getInstance(
                KeyProperties.KEY_ALGORITHM_AES,
                "AndroidKeyStore");
        generator.init(new KeyGenParameterSpec.Builder(
                keyId,
                KeyProperties.PURPOSE_ENCRYPT | KeyProperties.PURPOSE_DECRYPT)
                .setBlockModes(KeyProperties.BLOCK_MODE_GCM)
                .setEncryptionPaddings(KeyProperties.ENCRYPTION_PADDING_NONE)
                .setKeySize(128)
                .build());
        return generator.generateKey();
    }

    private static SecretKey generateSoftwareAesKey() throws Exception {
        KeyGenerator generator = KeyGenerator.getInstance("AES");
        generator.init(128);
        return generator.generateKey();
    }

    private static SecretKey deriveLegacyAesKey(char[] password) throws Exception {
        PBEKeySpec specification = new PBEKeySpec(
                password,
                new byte[] { 3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6 },
                1_000,
                128);
        try {
            SecretKeyFactory factory = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2WithHmacSHA1");
            return new SecretKeySpec(factory.generateSecret(specification).getEncoded(), "AES");
        } finally {
            specification.clearPassword();
        }
    }

    private static void assertSecretKeyEquals(SecretKey expected, SecretKey actual) {
        assertEquals(expected.getAlgorithm(), actual.getAlgorithm());
        assertArrayEquals(expected.getEncoded(), actual.getEncoded());
    }
}
","reason":"Adds focused instrumentation coverage for the coordinated current and legacy EncryptedKey contracts without modifying existing contract-pinning tests. It verifies AndroidKeyStore key creation/reload with the current three-argument and dual-key APIs, repeated current-record decryptability under one persistent alias, and retained legacy two-argument record decryption using PBKDF2-derived AES key material." ,"symbol":"EncryptedKey current-and-legacy compatibility test cases"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["The new instrumentation test calls EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) and decrypt(SecretKey) for retained legacy records.","The new instrumentation test calls EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String), isCurrentRecord(), getWrappingKeyId(), and decrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) for current records.","The test creates and reloads an AES/GCM AndroidKeyStore key, confirming current records remain decryptable after key reload."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey must retain the two-argument legacy encrypt/decrypt API and select the supplied legacy key for records without a current discriminator.","EncryptedKey must retain the current three-argument encrypt API, current-record accessors, and dual-key decrypt API used by this test.","Encryptor and MasterKey must continue to resolve the stored current wrapping-key identity to their persistent generated AndroidKeyStore key before calling dual-key decryption."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyTest.java","required_tests":["Run the Android instrumentation test task containing EncryptedKeyTest on an API level supporting AndroidKeyStore AES/GCM.","Verify current-record creation, AndroidKeyStore reload, and dual-key decryption through currentRecordRoundTripsAfterAndroidKeyStoreKeyReload.","Verify repeated current records decrypt after reload through repeatedCurrentRecordsDecryptWithTheSameReloadedAndroidKeyStoreKey.","Verify retained legacy two-argument encryption/decryption with PBKDF2-derived key material through legacyRecordEncryptedWithPbkdf2DerivedKeyRemainsDecryptable."]}
